    "result_text": "All 293 tests pass \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `locality` field on the owner-creation response. When an owner is created, `locality` is set to `local` if their city is the **single most common** city among the owners existing at that moment (strictly more owners than any other city \u2014 a tie or absence means `remote`), otherwise `remote`.\n\nChanges, following the existing pattern used for the other computed owner fields (`namesakeCount`, `sharesHousehold`, etc.):\n\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 computes locality (after city canonicalisation, before save) via a new `isMostCommonCity(...)` helper that groups existing owners by city case-insensitively, finds the max count, and requires a unique leader that matches the new owner's city.\n- **`model/Owner.java`** \u2014 added the `locality` field with getter/setter and `@Column` mapping.\n- **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `locality` string property to the `Owner` schema (drives the generated `OwnerDto`, which MapStruct maps automatically).\n- **Schema files** (hsqldb, h2, mysql, postgres) \u2014 added the `locality` column so it persists like the sibling fields.\n- **`OwnerRestControllerV1Tests`** \u2014 added two tests: `createOwnerInSingleMostCommonCityIsLocal` (5 owners pre-seeded in a unique city, exceeding the seed max of Madison=4, \u2192 `local`) and `createOwnerInUncommonCityIsRemote` (brand-new city \u2192 `remote`).\n\nOnly the V1 controller creates owners (V2 is read-only paging), so no change was needed there.",
